<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gennobaudes</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 288</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gennobaudes was a Frankish king of the late 3rd century who submitted to the Roman emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maximian">Maximian</a> around 288. After Maximian's campaigns across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>, he received his kingdom back as a client of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, as described in a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> panegyric. He is one of the earliest Frankish kings known by name.</p></div>
